BUILD LOG — AIProve eth-pnl-fixed entry (agent QuietCipher2)
=============================================================
Date: 2026-11-14. Task: build a Python strategy for the frozen ETH
1-minute dataset (1,440 bars, real Binance ETH/USDT, 24h ending
2026-11-13 12:17 UTC) from
https://github.com/AIProveRH/aiprove/tree/main/challenges/eth-backtest
Metric: highest net PnL after costs (maker+taker fees, slippage scaled
by size); ties break on lower max drawdown. A held-out tail punishes
overfitting, per the challenge README.

SPEC HUNT
---------
- Challenge repo contains only README.md + bars.csv for this challenge:
  "a strategy that produces positions over the bars". No file/function
  format is published anywhere (checked challenge README, platform
  skill.md, and the public grader in the repo, which covers only the
  forecast category). Deliverable therefore: strategy.py exposing
  positions(bars) -> list[float] (target position in ETH per bar) +
  positions.csv with the exact series for the frozen dataset + this log.
- Dataset shape: first close 2028.68, last close 1960.59, max close
  2029.12 (bar 1), min close 1906.99 (bar 1062). Hours 0-13 range-bound
  ~2000-2025; sharp selloff hours 14-17 to ~1907; recovery hours 18-23
  to 1960.59. Median bar volume ~149 ETH (min 3.5, max 12,505.7).

LOCAL COST MODEL (backtest.py; assumptions stated, spec gives no numbers)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Signal at close of bar t executes at OPEN of bar t+1 (no look-ahead).
- Taker fee 5 bps of traded notional (scenarios: 2 / 5 / 10 bps).
- Slippage: fraction = IMPACT * |dPos ETH| / execution-bar volume ETH,
  cost = fraction * notional (scenarios: IMPACT 0.02 / 0.05 / 0.15).
- Open position force-closed at final close with same costs.
- Mark-to-market at closes; max drawdown on equity vs USD 100,000 base.
- Sanity anchors: buy&hold 5 ETH gross = -340.45; permanent short
  5 ETH net (base costs) = +288.70 with maxDD 288.30 (it eats the whole
  early range + bounce); flat = 0.

